        {
            "block_label": "text",
            "block_content": "2. Delete doubled words. Early in the history of English, writers got into the habit of pairing a French or Latin word with a native English one because foreign words sounded more learned. Most paired words today are just redundant. Among the common ones:\nfull and complete    hope and trust    any and all\ntrue and accurate    each and every    basic and fundamental\nhope and desire    first and foremost    various and sundry",
            "block_bbox": [
                83,
                471,
                769,
                669
            ],
            "block_id": 8,
            "block_order": 7,
            "group_id": 8,
            "global_block_id": 8,
            "global_group_id": 8,
            "block_polygon_points": [
